     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A dose of 9,000 mg/day is in the range that causes acute liver injury. For a 70 kg patient, the toxicity threshold of about 150 mg/kg is roughly 10.5 g over 24 hours, and this order would nearly reach it every day. I can't think of an indication where this is safe or effective, and a nurse or pharmacist could give the doses before anyone catches the problem.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n\nIf the order is a typo, for example 3,000 mg/day meant as 1,000 mg three times daily, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it. If you have a clinical reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, it should go through pharmacy or toxicology review and be entered directly by you. I shouldn't enter it on my own."
      }
